      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "workspace-edge-semantic-aggregation"
        },
        "markdown": "# Detailed model notes\n\n## Rendering\n\nA bundle is shared routing geometry, not a replacement semantic edge. Draw every atomic edge as a parallel strand whenever screen spacing supports it. A single aggregate stroke is allowed only through an explicit presentation policy chosen because individual strands would be unreadable.\n\n## Labels\n\nShared-surface and bundle labels use the ordinary edge-label contract. A homogeneous bundle may display its common relationship label once. A heterogeneous bundle displays a count or summary while inspection exposes every constituent label.\n\n## Inspection\n\nEvery edge has a visual projection and stable logical identity. An edge may additionally carry data.relationshipRef pointing to an addressed graph that owns the claim's evidence, references, confidence, revision history, and discussion. Selecting an edge inspects local properties; opening the relationship navigates to that graph. Lightweight edges do not require a relationship graph."
      }
    },
