      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "title": "Inspectable Semantic Edge Bundles",
        "statement": "Keep relationships individually drawn inside shared routing bundles, reuse the edge-label contract for bundle labels, and let an edge navigate to an optional addressed relationship graph.",
        "status": "testing",
        "confidence": "plausible",
        "notes": "Bundling shares collectors and corridor geometry. It does not replace atomic strokes unless an explicit density policy determines that a single aggregate representation is more legible.\n\nFollow the labeled relationship ports in either direction. The Model port opens the separate detailed notes.",
